= New Ideas in the <span style="color: #c00000;">**SPD**</span>

The <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Nazis</span>' rise is unprecedented for a political party in modern Germany, and <span style="color: #c00000;">socialist</span> intellectuals are doing their best to come to terms with the rapid rise of this dangerous party. Among the mess of voices trying to push the party left or right, an unusual group has emerged, the "new revisionists" led by politican and activist Carlo Mierendorff. Basing its support primarily in the youth wing, they reject the <span style="color: #c00000;">Marxist Determinism</span> championed by the Center Marxists, Instead arguing that the <span style="color: #c00000;">**SPD**</span> should take action against the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Nazi</span> threat before it grows out of control.

Although the movement is still on the fringes of the party, it is rapidly gaining ground, namely with brand new propaganda tactics focused on emotion and symbols rather than reason - a tactic which eerily resembles the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">fascists</span>.

- @neorev_ideas

@neorev_ideas
title: Their ideas are put to test...
on-arrival: workers_kpd -= 1; unemployed_kpd -= 1; workers_nsdap -= 2; unemployed_nsdap -= 2; new_middle_nsdap -= 1; old_middle_nsdap -= 1; workers_spd += 3; unemployed_spd += 3; new_middle_spd += 2; old_middle_spd += 2; rural_spd += 4; neorevisionism_spd = 1

The <span style="color: #c00000;">**SPD**</span> incorporats the neorevisionist rhetoric into their propaganda with the "<span style="color: #c00000;">Three Arows</span>" being developed as an answer against the Nazi <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Swastika</span>, symbolizing opposition to <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Nazism</span>, <span style="color: #700000;">Stalinism</span> and <span style="color: #808080;">reaction</span>. The <span style="color: #c00000;">**SPD**</span> takes a breath of fresh air.
